o"><addressbook><name>KAMINAKA HIDEYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address> </addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC IND CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address> </addressbook> </applicant> <applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NEGI NORIYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NITTA YOSHIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKAMURA KAZUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMAMURA HARUNARI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUMITOMO METAL IND</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ABE, MASARU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAMINAKA, HIDEYA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC INDUSTRIAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NEGI, NORIYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NITTA, YOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKAMURA, KAZUHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMAMURA, HARUNARI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUMITOMO METAL INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ABE MASARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAMINAKA HIDEYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NEGI NORIYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NITTA YOSHIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKAMURA KAZUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMAMURA HARUNARI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ABE, MASARU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAMINAKA, HIDEYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NEGI, NORIYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NITTA, YOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKAMURA, KAZUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMAMURA, HARUNARI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A negative electrode material for a nonaqueous electrode secondary battery which comprises alloy grains comprising grains of Si phase (40) and, surrounding at least a part of each thereof, a solid solution or a phase of an intermetallic conpound of Si with another element selected from the group consisting of the elements belonging to Group 2A, the transition metal, Group 3B and Group 4B of the long term Periodic Table (for example, NiSi2 phase (42) and [NiSi2 + NiSi] phase (41)), and have an average particle diameter of 0.1 to 50  mu m, the grains of Si phase accounting for 5 to 99 wt.% of the material. The alloy grain can be produced by rapid solidification (for example, atomization or roll quenching) of a melt containing Si and another element mentioned above, or, by a method comprising subjecting a Si powder to electroless plating or mechanical alloying, to thereby deposit the other metal thereon and then subjecting the resultant product to heat-treating. This negative charge material can be used for producing a battery having a high discharge capacity and a long lifetime under the condition of use of repeating the charge-discharge cycle. Employment of a rapid solidification method allows the production of such an excellent material with no heat-treatment.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une matière d'électrode négative pour accumulateur secondaire à électrode non aqueuse, qui comporte des grains d'alliage contenant des grains de phase (40) de Si et, autour d'au moins une partie de chacun de ceux-ci, une solution solide ou une phase d'un composé intermétallique de Si et d'un autre élément sélectionné dans le groupe constitué par les éléments appartenant au groupe 2A, aux groupes 3B et 4B des métaux de transition de la classification périodique des éléments (par exemple, une phase (42) de NiSi2 et une phase (41) de [NiSi2 + NiSi]). La matière présente un diamètre moyen des particules se situant entre 0,1 et 50  mu m, les grains de la phase de Si représentant de 5 à 99 % en poids de la matière. Le grain d'alliage peut être produit par solidification rapide (par exemple par atomisation ou par refroidissement brusque de cylindre) d'un bain contenant du Si et un autre élément mentionné précédemment; ou par un procédé comportant les étapes consistant à soumettre une poudre de Si à un dépôt autocatalytique ou à une formation d'alliage mécanique pour permettre le dépôt de l'autre métal sur celle-ci, et soumettre ensuite le produit obtenu à un traitement thermique. Cette matière de charge négative peut être utilisée pour produire un accumulateur présentant une capacité de décharge élevée et une longue durée de vie dans des conditions d'utilisation impliquant une répétition du cycle charge/décharge. Le recours à un procédé de solidification rapide permet de produire cette excellente matière sans traitement thermique.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>